window.KGTeaching=[{"names":["Lomaharshana","Ugrashrava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"4 Ugrashrava, the son of Lomaharshana and the son of a suta,5 learned in the Puranas,6 and also known as Souti, once approached them, bowing in humility.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Parashara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"This learned brahmarshi, the son of Parashara, followed pure vows.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":72,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Janamejaya","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"When he was requested by Janamejaya and thousands of Brahmanas, he taught it to his disciple Vaishampayana, seated in his presence.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":77,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shuka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Dvaipayana first taught this index to his son Shuka and then to other disciples who had the same qualities.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":84,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"On seeing the sons of Pandu who had thus been left with them, the Kouravas, the learned among the castes and the townspeople exclaimed loudly with joy.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":97,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Indra","Sanjaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cO Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Arjuna, bound by his promise, had gone to heaven and learnt properly from Indra the use of celestial weapons.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":149,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"However, if a learned man recites this Veda of Krishna\u2019s,86 he will gain.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":254,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Karna","Krishna","Markandeya","Satya","Savitri"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Then there is the meeting with Markandeya and several stories, Krishna\u2019s meeting and conversation with Satya, the story of the measure of rice and that of Indradyumna and the accounts of Savitri, Ouddalaka and Vainya, the story of the Ramayana recounted at great length, the theft of Karna\u2019s earrings by Purandara,88 the account of the wood kindlings where Dharma teaches his son and where the Pandavas, after obtaining a boon, leave for the west.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":336,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"This sixth great parva of the Bharata is Bhishma Parva and was composed by Vyasa, learned in the Vedas, in 117 chapters and 5884 shlokas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":364,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gavalgana","Sanjaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"So did the learned and wise adviser Sanjaya, son of Gavalgana.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":424,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja","Narada","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Dharmaraja Yudhishthira met Narada and learnt from Narada about the destruction of the Vrishni lineage.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":425,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Lomaharshana","Shounaka","Ugrashrava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"41 Lomaharshana\u2019s son, the suta Ugrashrava, learned in ancient tales, was present at the twelve-year sacrifice of Kulapati Shounaka, held in Naimisharanya.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":4,"cited":true,"sentence_id":827,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shounaka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"5 Shounaka said, \u2018My son, in days long past, your father learnt all the Puranas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":841,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Lomaharshana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O son of Lomaharshana! Is it the case that you have learnt them too? In the Puranas are described divine stories and accounts of the wise of the original lineage.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":842,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Agni","Bhrigu","Indra","Maruts","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Souti said, \u2018That which was correctly learnt in ancient times by great- souled Brahmanas who were the best, that which was learnt and recited by the Brahmana Vaishampayana, that which was correctly studied by my father and from him learnt by me, O descendant of the Bhrigu race,2 hear that story of the Bhrigu lineage, revered by the gods, Indra, Agni and the Maruts.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":847,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Astika"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O supreme among the Brahmanas! This was Astika, chief among the Brahmanas, powerful in his austerities, brave, strong and learned in the Vedas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":11,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1042,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Lomaharshana","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"At the request of the Brahmanas, my learned father Lomaharshana, Vyasa\u2019s disciple and a suta, once narrated it.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":13,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1059,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kashyapa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Then the illustrious and learned Kashyapa, supreme among Brahmanas, revived through his learning the tree that had been reduced to a heap of ashes.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":39,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1973,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kashyapa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018The powerful Kashyapa then learnt through his divine knowledge that the life of the Pandava king had indeed been shortened.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":39,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1988,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Jaratkaru"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He is known as Jaratkaru and he is learned in the Vedas and the Vedangas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":41,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2050,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhrigu","Chyavana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He grew up in the house of the king of snakes and studied the Vedas and the Vedangas from the sage Chyavana, the son of Bhrigu.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":44,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2188,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Chyavana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The hotar was the Brahmana Chandabhargava, who was born in Chyavana\u2019s lineage and was famous as one who was learned in the Vedas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":48,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2341,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Learned in the use of arms, you are like Rama.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":50,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2453,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Janamejaya","Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"54 Souti said, \u2018Hearing that Janamejaya had been instated at the snake- sacrifice, the learned rishi Krishna Dvaipayana went there.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":54,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2586,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Janamejaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018Accompanied by his disciples, learned in the Vedas and the Vedangas, this great soul entered the sacrificial assembly of rajarshi Janamejaya.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":54,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2593,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vaishampayana","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 55 \u2018Vaishampayana said, \u201cBowing down first before my preceptor, with my mind and intellect concentrated and worshipping with devotion, reverence and single-mindedness all the Brahmanas and learned men, I shall now recite in its entirety the account I heard from the great-souled Vyasa, a wise maharshi famous in the three worlds, infinite in his accomplishments.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":55,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2610,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned man who recites it to others and also those who hear its recital attain the world of Brahma and become the equals of the gods.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":56,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2666,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Paila","Shuka","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"59 The greatest lord and granter of boons then taught the Vedas and the fifth Veda Mahabharata to Sumantu, Jaimini, Paila, his own son Shuka and his disciple Vaishampayana.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2801,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Being thus cursed, Dharma was born in the womb of a Shudra in the form of Vidura, learned, righteous and pure of body.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2813,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhima","Bhimasena","Dhritarashtra","Kali","Narada","Pradyumna","Suparna","Ugrasena","Varuna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018O king! Bhimasena, Ugrasena, Suparna, Varuna, Gopati, Dhritarashtra, Suryavarcha the seventh, Pattravan, Arkaparna, the famous Prayuta, Bhima, Chitraratha, all famous and learned in all matters, Shalishira, Pradyumna the fourteenth, Kali the fifteenth and Narada the sixteenth, these divine gandharvas are known as the sons of Muni.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":59,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2967,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Devala"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Devala himself had two sons who were learned and forgiving.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":60,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3016,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhrigu","Shukra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Bhrigu\u2019s son was the learned Shukra, wise and the son of one who was wise, and a planet.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":60,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3039,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhrigu","Chyavana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Bhrigu had another son named Chyavana, learned, righteous and radiant in his austerities.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":60,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3044,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The youngest was Bhishma, intelligent, learned in the Vedas, the best of speakers, fearful to enemy armies and the dispeller of fear among the Kurus.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":61,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3146,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In other places, Brahmanas learned in the science of tones recited other mantras, so that all these holy sounds made the hermitage seem like the illustrious world of Brahma.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":64,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3311,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shakuntala"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Shakuntala said, \u201cO king! Then listen to how I have learnt what occurred in earlier times and how I came to be the sage\u2019s daughter.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":65,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3348,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Daksha","Narada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In an assembly of these 1000 of Daksha\u2019s sons, Narada taught them the supreme philosophy of sankhya,129 the means to salvation.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":70,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3722,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Ila","Pururava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018The learned Pururava was born from Ila and it is said that she was both his father and mother.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":70,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3738,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"However, though immensely learned, Brihaspati could not revive them.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":71,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3804,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kacha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"They learnt the knowledge that Kacha had learnt and were content.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":73,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3960,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Nahusha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Having learnt that she was the daughter of a Brahmana, the king, who was Nahusha\u2019s son, grasped her by the right hand and pulled her out of the well.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":73,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3994,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yayati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"How can a proud one like me allow any other man to touch my hand?\u201d Yayati replied, \u201cThe learned men know that a Brahmana is more to be avoided than a virulently poisonous and angry snake or a blazing fire that spreads in all directions.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":76,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4122,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shakuntala"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"From him, and through Shakuntala, was born a learned son named Bharata who became the king.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":89,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4708,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhimasena","Chitrasena","Parikshit","Sushena","Ugrasena"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Parikshit had sons who were learned in dharma and artha\u2014Kakshasena, Ugrasena, the immensely valorous Chitrasena, Indrasena, Sushena and Bhimasena.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":89,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4756,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vashishtha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He has studied the Vedas and the Vedangas from Vashishtha himself.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":94,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5155,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Satyavati","Vichitravirya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The one who was learned in dharma accomplished this superhuman deed in accordance with dharma and began to make arrangements for his brother Vichitravirya\u2019s marriage, following the consultation with Satyavati.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":96,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5328,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Amba","Kashi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"After consulting the Brahmanas, who were learned in the Vedas, the one who had knowledge about dharma, gave permission to Amba, the eldest daughter of the king of Kashi, to leave.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":96,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5335,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati","Utathya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O illustrious Brihaspati! Utathya\u2019s son is in my womb and has studied the Vedas and the Vedangas there.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":98,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5407,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bali"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"One day, a king named Bali, who was learned in all aspects of dharma, had come to the water and saw him floating along in the current.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":98,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5425,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"As a consequence of the curse imposed by the great-souled Mandavya, Dharma himself was born as Vidura and he was learned in all principles and free from anger and desire.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":100,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5568,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kunti","Pandu","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 112 Vaishampayana said, \u2018O king! Having been thus addressed, Kunti told Pandu, bull among the Kurus, lord of the earth and her husband, \u201cO one who is learned in the law! O one with eyes like those of a blue lotus! You should not speak in this way to me.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":112,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6024,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bharadvaja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The powerful Bharadvaja, supreme among those who know dharma, taught the knowledge of the agneya weapon to the illustrious Agniveshya.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":121,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6542,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018Drona said, \u201cDesiring to learn the science of Dhanur Veda, I earlier went to maharshi Agniveshya.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":122,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6612,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Panchala","Yajnasena"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The powerful Yajnasena, son of the king of Panchala, hardworking and dedicated, also studied with me under that teacher.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":122,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6614,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona","Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018Then the valorous Drona taught Pandu\u2019s sons the use of many weapons, human and divine.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":122,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6644,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O bull among the Bharata lineage! Other princes also came to Drona, supreme among Brahmanas, to learn the use of arms\u2014the Vrishnis, the Andhakas, kings from many countries and Radheya,344 the son of the suta.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":122,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6645,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Drona"],"teacher":"Drona","student":"Arjuna","text":"\u201d Then Drona taught Arjuna the art of fighting from horses, elephants, chariots and on the ground.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":123,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6657,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":false},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"However, since he was the son of a nishada,346 Drona, who was learned in dharma, thought about it and refused to accept him as a student of archery, out of consideration for the others.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":123,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6662,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kunti","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Vidura, learned in all aspects of dharma, revived the unconscious Kunti by sprinkling water scented with sandalwood over her.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":126,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6916,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kunti"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 148 \u2018Kunti said, \u201cI wish to learn exactly from you the reason for this grief.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":148,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7727,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"9 From that was born a son, who became the learned Drona and who studied all the Vedas and the Vedangas.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":154,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7893,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drupada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Drupada said, \u2018A man without learning cannot be a friend to one who is learned, nor one without chariots to one who has chariots, nor one who is not a king to one who is a king.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":154,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7907,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Tapati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O descendant of Tapati\u2019s lineage! Therefore, men should always employ priests who are learned and self-controlled in all acts that are desired.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":159,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8166,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Samvarana","Surya","Tapati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"On seeing that Samvarana was learned in the path of dharma and was unparalleled on earth for his handsomeness, Surya decided that he was the best husband for Tapati.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":160,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8191,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vashishtha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Then, seeing that condition, the illustrious rishi Vashishtha, learned in dharma, went to the supreme among kings.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":163,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8295,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vashishtha","Vishvamitra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cWhen Vashishtha learnt that Vishvamitra had conspired to get his sons killed, he bore his grief patiently, like a great mountain bears the earth.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":166,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8431,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Ikshvaku"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O best among the twice-born! O best among those who are learned in the Vedas! I wish to obtain a boon from you, so that I can be freed from the debt I owe to the Ikshvaku lineage.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":168,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8487,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Parashara","Shakti"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"But the immensely energetic Parashara, Shakti\u2019s son and chief among those who were learned in the Vedas, performed a rakshasa sacrifice.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":172,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8612,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Kalmashapada","King","Vashishtha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 173 \u2018Arjuna said, \u201cWhy did King Kalmashapada himself call and instruct his wife to go to his preceptor, supreme among those who are learned in the Vedas? Why did the great-souled maharshi Vashishtha, who knew the path of supreme dharma, agree to go to a woman who was forbidden? Why were these acts done earlier? I wish to know.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":173,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8635,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Tell"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Tell us who, learned in the Vedas, is fit to be appointed our priest.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":174,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8668,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Dhritarashtra","Drona","Shantanu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 198 \u2018Dhritarashtra said, \u201cShantanu\u2019s son, the learned Bhishma, the illustrious rishi Drona and you yourself have spoken the truth and that which is best for me.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":198,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9514,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drupada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! Having gone there, that righteous man, learned in all the shastras, addressed Drupada appropriately and waited on him.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":198,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9526,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drupada","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"199 \u2018Drupada said, \u201cO greatly learned Vidura! It is indeed as you have told me now.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":199,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9550,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gada","Kritavarma","Pradyumna","Samba","Satyaki"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Satyaka, Satyaki, the Satvata Kritavarma, Pradyumna, Samba, Nishatha, Shanku, the valorous Charudeshna, Jhilli, Viprithu, mighty-armed Sarana and Gada, supreme among those who are learned\u2014these and many other Vrishnis, Bhojas and Andhakas went to Khandavaprastha, carrying many gifts with them.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":213,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10155,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"That vanquisher of enemies learned all the vedas from Arjuna, with the four divisions and the ten branches, and the art of archery, everything known to man and god.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":213,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10199,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"33 After having studied the vedas, these observers of rigid vows learnt the use of all weapons, human and divine, from Arjuna.","parva":"01_Adi","chapter":213,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10226,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned and strong one then went to the other brothers with Partha.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":50,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"36 At Tumbaru\u2019s command, those learned ones sang in celestial tones, as was laid down in the rules, and pleasured and paid homage to Pandu\u2019s sons and the rishis who were assembled in the sabha, rigid in their vows and devoted to the truth.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":4,"cited":true,"sentence_id":138,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Having been thus worshipped by all the Pandavas, the great rishi who was learned in the Vedas asked Yudhishthira questions mixed with dharma, artha and kama.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":146,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"What were his deeds, traits, austerities and rigidity of vows that this famous one alone rivals Shakra? O brahmana! When you went to the world of the ancestors, did you see the immensely fortunate Pandu, my father? O illustrious lord! What did he say? I wish to learn.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":11,"cited":true,"sentence_id":343,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Having heard of Dharmaraja\u2019s sacrifice and learned about sacrifices, they happily set out, with the brahmanas at the forefront.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":31,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1295,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Amba","Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Bhishma! Which learned one, with dharma in his heart and supreme among all learned ones, will act as you have, ignoring the precepts of dharma? \u2018\u201cO Bhishma! If you think you know dharma and think yourself to be wise in intelligence, why did you abduct the maiden Amba? She desired someone else.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":38,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1527,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cO Bhishma! Learned men in ancient times told this story.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":38,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1545,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra","Jamadagni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Just as the saptarshis approach the great Indra, lord of the gods, in heaven, with Jamadagni\u2019s son,95 the great-souled ones, learned in the Vedas and the mantras, came with large quantities of gifts.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":49,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2063,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Vidura","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Then Dhritarashtra, lord of men, spoke to the learned Vidura, foremost among his advisers, \u201cGo to Prince Yudhishthira and swiftly bring him here at my command.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":51,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2170,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Vidura, supreme among learned ones, did not approve of his brother\u2019s words and thought them to be unjust.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":51,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2174,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shakuni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Why do you then praise playing with the dice? O Shakuni! The learned do not praise deceitful gambling.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":53,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2257,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shakuni","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Shakuni said, \u201cO Yudhishthira! The learned triumph over non-learned only through trickery.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":53,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2273,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 280(55) \u2018Vidura said, \u201cO great king!146 Listen to what I am going to tell you and learn, even though a dying man finds no pleasure in medicine.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":55,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2362,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In a soft voice, Krishna whispered again, \u201cThere are those in the assembly hall who are learned in the sacred texts.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":60,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2651,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Then Vidura, learned in all the ways of dharma, raised his arms and silenced those who were in the assembly hall.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":61,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2770,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Angirasa","Prahlada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In this context, the learned ones quote the ancient conversation that took place between Prahlada and the sage who was the son of Angirasa.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":61,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2780,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Prahlada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Prahlada said, \u2018O illustrious one! You are learned in the ways of dharma, for the gods, the demons and the brahmanas.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":61,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2789,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Duhshasana","Janamejaya","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"291(66) Janamejaya asked, \u2018When they learnt that the Pandavas had been granted permission to leave with their gems, riches and treasures, what was the state of mind of Dhritarashtra\u2019s sons?\u2019 Vaishampayana said, \u2018O king! When he found out that the intelligent Dhritarashtra had given the permission, Duhshasana swiftly went to his brother.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":66,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3017,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati","Duryodhana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018Duryodhana said, \u201cO king! Have you not heard what Brihaspati, the learned priest of the gods, told Shakra about policy? \u2018O destroyer of enemies! Enemies must be killed through every means possible, before they cause harm through war or force.","parva":"02_Sabha","chapter":66,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3022,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shounaka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018There was a learned brahmana named Shounaka.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":108,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kunti","Shounaka","Vaishampayana","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 300(3) Vaishampayana said, \u2018Having heard these words of Shounaka, Kunti\u2019s son Yudhishthira went to his priest and in the midst of his brothers, said, \u201cThese brahmanas are learned in the Vedas.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":3,"cited":true,"sentence_id":227,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned Vidura is a well-wisher of the sons of Pandu and is always devoted to their welfare.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":8,"cited":true,"sentence_id":416,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Duryodhana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"If you have compassion for the Kouravas, teach my evil-souled son Duryodhana.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":11,"cited":true,"sentence_id":510,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Pandu\u2019s son! O best of the Kurus! When I reached Dvaraka, I learnt everything about your misfortunes from Yuyudhana.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":14,"cited":true,"sentence_id":915,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kouravya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kouravya! On returning there, I learnt everything that the evilminded and evil-souled king of Marttikavata had said about me.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":15,"cited":true,"sentence_id":945,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shalva","Soubha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O tiger among men! I learnt there that Shalva had left the city on Soubha.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":21,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1169,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Dharmaraja! You are ours and where are you going, leaving us and that?\u201d Then energetic Bibhatsu, learned in dharma, kama and artha, spoke in a loud voice to the gathering, \u201cThe king will make his home in the forest so as to rob the enemies of all their fame.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":24,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1363,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja","Dhritarashtra","Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018The beloved, beautiful, learned and devoted Krishna spoke these words to Dharmaraja, \u201cThere is no sorrow over us in the mind of that evil, cruel and evil-minded son of Dhritarashtra.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":28,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1472,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"That immensely wise Indra of the asuras was one to whom all knowledge of dharma had been imparted.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":29,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1520,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja","Satyavati","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Having thus spoken, the illustrious lord, Satyavati\u2019s intelligent son Vyasa who was learned in yoga, taught Dharmaraja, who had purified himself, that supreme knowledge of yoga.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":37,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2195,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O great king! Just as the rishis follow Indra of the gods, the brahmana ascetics, learned in words and sounds, followed him.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":37,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2200,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d253 Having uttered these words, the lord Dharmaraja imparted the knowledge to him, after he was consecrated according to the rites and controlled in speech, body and mind.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":38,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2231,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Chitrasena","Kounteya","Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"When Partha became skilled in the use of all weapons and the right time had come, Shakra told him, \u201cO Kounteya! Now learn singing and dancing from Chitrasena.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":45,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2643,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kounteya! If you learn this, it will bring your own welfare.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":45,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2645,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Nala"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He had a son named Nala, learned in the ways of dharma and artha.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":49,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2885,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihatsena","Nala","Punyashloka","Varshneya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"When she learnt that the dice were always being unfavourable towards Punyashloka and that Nala had lost all his possessions, she told her nurse, \u2018O Brihatsena! O fortunate one! As if on Nala\u2019s instructions, go again and bring the suta Varshneya here.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3184,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kali","Karkotaka","Nala"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cWhen Nala had learned the knowledge of the dice, Kali emerged from his body, continuously vomiting from his mouth Karkotaka\u2019s virulent venom.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":70,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4079,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rituparna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! At last, a learned brahmana named Parnada discovered you in Koshala, in Rituparna\u2019s house.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":75,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4287,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Uma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"One who is learned in dharma should then go to the sacred place of Uma\u2019s consort.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":80,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4585,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Yudhishthira!53 O one learned in dharma! He then goes on to Arbuda, the son of the Himalayas.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":80,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4593,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra","Vishnu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"113 O one learned in dharma! O Indra among kings! One then goes to Vishnu\u2019s supreme region.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":81,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4703,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pulastya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d\u2019220 379(82) \u2018\u201cPulastya said, \u2018O one learned in dharma! One should then go to the ancient Dharmatirtha.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":82,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4991,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among kings! On going to the confluence of the Ganga with the ocean, the learned have said that one obtains ten times a horse sacrifice.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":83,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5212,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Angiras"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Seated on the upper garments of the maharshis, the son of the sage Angiras taught them and pronounced the syllables of \u2018OM\u2019, accurately and as they should be uttered.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":83,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5264,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The brahmanas who are knowledgeable in the Vedas and those who are learned about the nature of the soul say that the great-souled Krishna is the eternal dharma.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":86,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5471,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Thus Kounteya has become skilled in weapons and has learnt gandharva veda.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":89,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5559,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"They then went to Mahidhara, worshipped by rajarshi Gaya, unrivalled in radiance, learned in dharma and the performer of pure deeds.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":93,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5703,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya","Lomasha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d \u2018Lomasha said, \u201cO Kounteya! The king was learned in supreme dharma.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":131,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7335,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018\u201cThe hawk said, \u2018O one learned in dharma! I am Indra and that dove is the bearer of the sacrificial offerings.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":131,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7340,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Ashtavakra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cAshtavakra said, \u2018I have heard that, vanquishing learned brahmanas in debate, this one immersed them in water.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":134,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7556,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra","Yavakrita","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Yudhishthira! Indra went to Yavakrita and asked him, \u2018Why are you engaged in these supreme torments?\u2019 Yavakrita replied, \u2018O one who is worshipped by the masses of gods! I am performing this supreme austerity so that the Vedas, studied by brahmanas, become manifest in me.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":135,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7632,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Raibhya","Yavakrita"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O supreme among the immortals! Using that particular rite, how was it that Raibhya was capable of slaying a learned ascetic like me?\u2019 The gods replied, \u2018O Yavakrita! O sage! Do not think it is the way you have spoken.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":139,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7795,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhima","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 442(145) \u2018Yudhishthira said, \u201cO Bhima! This bull among rakshasas is learned in dharma.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":145,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8032,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O unblemished one! Together with Krishna and his brothers, and the brahmanas who were learned in the Vedas and the Vedangas, the Pandava happily entered the pure place that was like heaven itself.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":145,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8106,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhoumya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In that fashion, Dhoumya, learned in dharma and the priest of the Pandavas, approached the rishi who was rigid in his vows, in accordance with propriety.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":156,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8905,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Through his divine sight, the sage who was learned in dharma had already recognized Pandu\u2019s sons, the best of the Kuru lineage, and greeting them, asked them to be seated.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":156,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8906,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhoumya","Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201cDoes your mind ever turn towards that which is not true or do you follow dharma? O Partha! Does your conduct towards your mother and father ever diminish? Are your preceptors, all the elders and those who are learned worshipped by you? O Partha! Does your mind ever turn towards evil acts? O best of the Kuru lineage! Do you know how to reward a good deed and ignore an evil deed? Do you treat them according to the law and without any conceit? Do virtuous ones rejoice when such deserving ones are honoured by you? Though you dwell in the forest, do you follow that which is dharma? O Partha! Has Dhoumya been tormented by the way you treat him? Do you follow the dharma of donations, austerities, purity, uprightness and forbearance? O Partha! Do you follow the conduct of your fathers and grandfathers? O Pandava! Do you tread the path followed by the rajarshis? It is said that when a son or a grandson is born in one\u2019s lineage, the ancestors in the world of the ancestors either sorrow or laugh.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":156,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8909,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["King"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O son!131 Learned rishis, knowledgeable in dharma have said that this is the abode of Mahendra and King Vaishravana.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":160,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9179,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shiva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201cI have learnt these weapons from Shakra, the wind-god and Shiva themselves.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":161,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9277,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Matali"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d \u2018Arjuna said, \u201cO lord! Having learnt that they could not be slain by the gods and the asuras, I happily told Matali, \u2018Go swiftly to that city.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":170,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9707,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanatkumara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 On hearing this, the great-souled sages swiftly went to Sanatkumara to resolve the doubt, because he was learned in dharma.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":183,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10494,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhargava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O best among the Bhargava lineage! I wish to learn about this.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":192,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11478,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O immensely radiant one! Brahma, the Vedas and all that is capable of being learnt has been created by you.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":192,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11489,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shakuni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Shakuni said, \u201cThe eldest Pandava is learned in dharma.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":228,"cited":true,"sentence_id":13824,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d O destroyer of enemies! The learned Vidura, devoted to dharma, entertained all the varnas, as he had been instructed.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":242,"cited":true,"sentence_id":14472,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Lakshmana","Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He had four sons who were learned in dharma and artha\u2014 Rama, Lakshmana, Shatrughna and the immensely strong Bharata.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":258,"cited":true,"sentence_id":15237,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O descendant of the Bharata lineage! He consulted his advisers and the priests, who were learned about dharma, about instating Rama as the heir apparent.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":261,"cited":true,"sentence_id":15367,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vaidehi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cWhen all of them had left, a rakshasi named Trijata, who was learned about dharma and pleasant in speech, comforted Vaidehi.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":264,"cited":true,"sentence_id":15686,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Then, together with Rama, you will learn about the great service I have rendered.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":266,"cited":true,"sentence_id":15810,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Goutama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Goutama said, \u2018I have studied the Vedas, together with their branches, and I have accumulated great austerities.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":282,"cited":true,"sentence_id":16908,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Surya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Through his powers of yoga, Surya assumed the form of a handsome brahmana, learned in the Vedas.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":284,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17022,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kunti"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Kunti replied, \u201cO foremost among those who are learned in the Vedas! All my desires have already been satisfied, since you and my father are pleased with me.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":289,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17232,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vibhavasu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Vibhavasu! I summoned you to learn about the strength of the mantra.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":290,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17290,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"33 There, he went to Drona to learn about weapons.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":293,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17421,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Hari","Narayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"But the one you seek to kill is protected by a great-souled one who is known as the unvanquished boar,38 Hari and the inconceivable Narayana by those who are learned in the Vedas.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":294,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17476,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Janamejaya","Tell"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Janamejaya asked, \u2018Where did the brave Pandavas reside? How did they learn about these glad tidings? What did they do when the twelve years had passed? O illustrious one! Tell me everything about all this.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":294,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17498,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018The yaksha asked, \u201cHow does one become learned? How does one attain greatness? O king! How does one obtain a second? How does one become intelligent?\u201d \u2018Yudhishthira replied, \u201cOne becomes learned through the sacred texts.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":297,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17676,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Hari","Vritra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"36 O one learned in dharma! You have heard how Hari hid himself in Shakra\u2019s vajra so that Vritra might be killed.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":299,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17842,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhoumya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The five learned Pandavas arose with Dhoumya.","parva":"03_Aranyaka","chapter":299,"cited":true,"sentence_id":17858,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Virata"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"22 O king! I will teach the women in Virata\u2019s abode these arts.","parva":"04_Virata","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":87,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Unless I know the truth, how can I judge skilfully?\u201d Having learnt what had happened, those present in the assembly honoured Krishna a lot.","parva":"04_Virata","chapter":15,"cited":true,"sentence_id":679,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gandhara","Krishna","Shakuni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Will you fight with Pandava the way you gambled and won Indraprastha and the way you dragged Krishna to the assembly hall? This wise uncle of yours, Shakuni of Gandhara,115 is a deceitful gambler and is learned about the dharma of kshatriyas.","parva":"04_Virata","chapter":45,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2156,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Prajapati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"I have learnt from Prajapati deep, terrible and wonderful techniques.","parva":"04_Virata","chapter":56,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2627,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Drona","Duryodhana","Shantanu","Tell"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Tell him the words that he should speak\u2014how Duryodhana is to be addressed, and the king who is Shantanu\u2019s son, how Dhritarashtra is to be addressed, and Drona, supreme among learned ones.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":4,"cited":true,"sentence_id":160,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vishnu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"With the enemy having been slain, Vasava was delighted, and together with the gods, showed his homage to Vishnu, who is learned in dharma and is supreme in the three worlds.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":10,"cited":true,"sentence_id":549,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Duryodhana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O learned one! Duryodhana will not give up even one foot of ground because of fear.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":21,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1087,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Bhishma","Drona","Kripa","Krishna","Satyaki","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"I have heard that Satyaki learnt about weapons from Drona, Arjuna, Vasudeva, Kripa and Bhishma and that he is an equal of Krishna\u2019s son.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":22,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1168,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned Krishna is the lord of dharma.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":28,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1435,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Tell"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O learned one! Tell me completely and truthfully about everything that Ajatashatru desires.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":34,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2075,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Dhritarashtra asked, \u201cThe gods desire those who have been born in great lineages, those who are extremely learned and are always devoted to dharma and artha.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":36,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2378,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Sanatsujata"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018Dhritarashtra asked, \u201cO Sanatsujata! I have heard about your teaching that death does not exist.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":42,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2906,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 706(43) \u2018Dhritarashtra asked, \u201cThere may be a brahmana who has learnt the chants of the Rig, the Yajur and the Sama Veda.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":43,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2984,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanatsujata"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"If he performs a sin, will he be tainted, or will he not be tainted?\u201d \u2018Sanatsujata replied, \u201cOne who is learned in the chants of the Sama, the Rig and the Yajur will not be saved from his evil deeds.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":43,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2985,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Sanatsujata"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Dhritarashtra asked, \u201cO learned one! If the Vedas are incapable of saving one who is without dharma, why have the brahmanas eternally talked about them?\u201d \u2018Sanatsujata replied, \u201cThe austerities performed in this world are seen to yield fruits in another.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":43,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2990,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"It is through such brahmacharya that the gods attained divinity, the immensely fortunate and learned rishis attained the world of Brahma and the gandharvas and the apsaras obtained their beauty.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":44,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3076,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dasharha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"35 Embracing Govinda, he said, \u201cO Dasharha! O immensely radiant one! The devarshis who are the performers of good deeds, the extremely learned brahmanas, the rajarshis and the venerable ascetics once witnessed the ancient battle between the gods and the asuras.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":81,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5252,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"After having studied all the Vedas, they attained Yama\u2019s abode.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":107,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6599,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Suparna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d\u2019 772(109) \u2018\u201cSuparna said, \u2018Since one is absolved from sins and obtains supreme welfare, learned ones therefore refer to it as the northern direction.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":109,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6637,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Krishna","Vaishampayana","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 790(127) Vaishampayana said, \u2018When Dhritarashtra, lord of men, heard Krishna\u2019s words, he quickly spoke to Vidura, learned in all manner of dharma.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":127,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7418,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna","Madhava","Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cO Krishna! O Madhava! Speak these words to the fortunate and illustrious Krishna,317 learned in all forms of dharma and daughter-in- law of the great-souled Pandu.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":135,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8001,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cVasudeva said, \u2018O Radheya! You have served brahmanas who are learned in the Vedas.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":138,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8140,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Madhusudana! The learned ones have said that these are the signs of the defeat of the entire army of Dhritarashtra\u2019s son.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":141,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8314,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kali"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O great king! The citizens, my fortunate mother Kali, the servants, the priests, the preceptors and the extremely learned brahmanas were greatly distressed and kept urging me, \u201cBe our king.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":145,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8553,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bharadvaja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He learnt the use of weapons from Bharadvaja.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":149,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8778,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"8 O great king! In marching troops out, in engaging in battle and in pacifying enemies, I am learned, as learned as Brihaspati himself.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":162,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9504,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! O Bhishma! Especially because you are a Kourava, how can you, who have studied the sacred texts, make someone like that live in this household? O bull among the Bharata lineage! Now that you know this, make up your mind about what should be done.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":171,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9981,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhargava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"But will I be able to see that arya, famous in the world? How will Bhargava destroy my terrible misery? I wish to learn about this and I will go there after that.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":174,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10126,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kashi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018O descendant of Kashi! O one who is beautiful in complexion! I do not voluntarily take up weapons, except for the sake of those who are learned about the brahman.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":177,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10248,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Akritavrana","Bhargava"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"His friend Akritavrana, learned in the Vedas and beloved of Bhargava, acted as his charioteer.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":180,"cited":true,"sentence_id":10425,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhrishtadyumna","Parshata","Shikhandi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Shikhandi, the son of a king, together with Parshata Dhrishtadyumna and all of you, learnt the four parts of Dhanurveda.","parva":"05_Udyoga","chapter":193,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11163,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanjaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Sanjaya replied, \u201cO great king! Because everything in the earth is based on the five universal constituents, the learned regard all of them as equal.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":6,"cited":true,"sentence_id":315,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kouravya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kouravya! The learned have said that there are seven varshas there.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":12,"cited":true,"sentence_id":663,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kounteya! Even if a learned man takes care, the turbulent senses violently steal his mind.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":24,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1515,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kounteya! Learn briefly from me how one who has attained liberation attains the brahman.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":40,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2457,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanjaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Sanjaya replied, \u201cO descendant of the Bharata lineage! When the forenoon of that day had passed and when the great-souled Pandavas were delighted at having accomplished victory, your father, Devavrata, learned in all kinds of dharma, advanced on the swiftest of steeds towards the army of the Pandavas.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":55,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3693,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O son!201 In earlier times, the learned rishis spoke about Vasudeva in their assembly and I heard this.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":62,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4537,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Having heard the nature of the great-souled and illustrious Vasudeva, the lord of the lords of the worlds and the undecaying one, from whom was created Brahma, the father of the universe, why should men not worship and show obeisance to Vasudeva? O son! You have been restrained earlier by the sages, learned in the Vedas, and been asked not to enter into a fight with the intelligent Vasudeva and also with the Pandavas.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":62,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4539,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Ananta","Shesha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He created the god Shesha, whom the learned know of as Ananta.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":63,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4598,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"From Drona, he had learnt about releasing and withdrawing extremely difficult weapons.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":69,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4901,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Tell"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018O one who is learned in dharma! How will we obtain victory and the kingdom? How can this destruction of subjects be stopped? O lord! Tell us this.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":103,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7757,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Bhishma, the best of the Bharata lineage and learned about dharma and artha, was satisfied and praised Dhananjaya for having given him that pillow.","parva":"06_Bhishma","chapter":115,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9059,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Other than you, who among the kings is capable of fighting with Arjuna on the field of battle? The learned ones speak about his celestial deeds.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":3,"cited":true,"sentence_id":215,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna","Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018\u201cDrona replied, \u2018O son!3 You and Arjuna are equal in what you have learned from your teachers.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":52,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3558,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Vasudeva spoke these words to the unvanquished and learned Bibhatsu and he spoke these meaningful words in return.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3919,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rudra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"They were learned in the Vedas and chanted one hundred hymns in praise of the brahman and Rudra.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4032,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona","Indra","Kripa","Partha","Rudra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Is this what the great-minded Indra instructed you himself? O Partha! Are these the weapons you learnt from Rudra, Drona and Kripa? It is said that you know more about dharma than anyone else in this world.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":118,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8826,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Hidimba","Karna","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"11 O learned one! Like that, I think that Vasudeva has gained from the battle between Karna and Hidimba\u2019s son.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":157,"cited":true,"sentence_id":12310,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d\u2019 CHAPTER 1146(169) \u2018Dhritarashtra said, \u201cThe great-souled one had studied the Vedas and their branches in the proper way.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":169,"cited":true,"sentence_id":13738,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! Having fought for five days and having killed many soldiers, the brahmana, learned in the Vedas, went to Brahma\u2019s world.","parva":"07_Drona","chapter":172,"cited":true,"sentence_id":14272,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhargava","Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Bhargava gave supreme weapons to the great-souled one and when he was a child, Rama himself taught him Dhanurveda.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":1,"cited":true,"sentence_id":79,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Drona","Jamadagni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"96 The brave one ignored maharathas like Bhishma and Drona and learnt the extremely terrible brahmastra from Jamadagni\u2019s son.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":508,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhargava","Karna"],"teacher":"Bhargava","student":"Karna","text":"\u2018 \u201c\u2018Bhargava imparted all his knowledge of dhanurveda to the great-souled Karna, tiger among men, having been extremely pleased with him.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":24,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2558,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":false},{"names":["Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O learned one! Therefore, I will advance against Partha.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":26,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2687,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned leader arrayed it well, according to the norms of Brihaspati.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":31,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3400,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The one who was learned in the use of weapons invoked his arrows with the mantras of divine weapons and surrounded Yudhishthira in the battle.","parva":"08_Karna","chapter":39,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4129,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The great-minded king of the Kurus also grasped a beautiful bow and displayed the diverse kinds of learning that he had been taught by Drona.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":15,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1276,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Let the lord of the earth learn about Krishna\u2019s greatness today.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":18,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1644,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhisthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018 \u201cYudhisthira said, \u2018O Suyodhana! It is through good fortune that you have learnt about the dharma of kshatriyas.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":31,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3000,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pushkara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Thus, for the sake of the grandfather and to satisfy the learned ones, Sarasvati, supreme among rivers, manifested herself in Pushkara.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":37,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3552,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Devala","Janamejaya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Janamejaya! However, when it was time to take food, the intelligent mendicant, learned in dharma, presented himself before Devala.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":49,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4598,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Janamejaya","Vaishampayana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 Janamejaya asked, \u2018In ancient times, during the twelve years of drought, why did the sage Sarasvata, rich in austerities, teach the Vedas?\u2019 Vaishampayana replied, \u2018O great king! In earlier times, there was an intelligent sage who was a great ascetic.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":50,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4687,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhima","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018 \u201cVasudeva replied, \u2018They are equal in what they have learnt, but Bhima is stronger.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5203,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Duryodhana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018 \u201cDuryodhana said, \u2018I have studied and given the ordained gifts.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":60,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5527,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Pandu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"If victory is obtained unfairly, what pleasure can virtuous men obtain from that? Which learned one will approve this violation of rules? Having obtained victory through adharma, learned ones do not rejoice in the way that the wicked Vrikodara, Pandu\u2019s son, is delighted.","parva":"09_Shalya","chapter":63,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5774,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"How do learned ones free themselves from their mental grief, when they come in contact with something that is injurious, or when they are separated from something that is good?\u201d \u2018Vidura replied, \u201cWhenever the mind is free from unhappiness and happiness\u2014that is when a learned one obtains peace and attains a good objective.","parva":"11_Stri","chapter":3,"cited":true,"sentence_id":138,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gavalgana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned suta, Gavalgana\u2019s son,19 seized him and asked him not to act in this way.","parva":"11_Stri","chapter":11,"cited":true,"sentence_id":497,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Drona"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Drona was placed on this and those who were learned about samas chanted the three samas.","parva":"11_Stri","chapter":23,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1158,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He is asked to learn about dharma from Bhishma and enters Hastinapura.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":null,"cited":false,"sentence_id":9,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":"Bhishma","student":"Yudhishthira","text":"Bhishma teaches Yudhishthira about raja dharma, the dharma of the four varnas and the four ashramas.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":null,"cited":false,"sentence_id":11,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":true},{"names":["Angirasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He went to the best of the Angirasa lineage, your preceptor,9 to learn about the science of war.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":96,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Jarasandha","Karna","King","Narada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1333(5) \u2018Narada said, \u201cHaving learnt about Karna\u2019s strength, King Jarasandha, the lord of Magadha, challenged him to a duel.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":234,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arjuna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Arjuna! This being the case, why are you praising wealth, which is harmful? O descendant of the Bharata lineage! In earlier times, there were people who could see and were learned in the sacred texts.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":19,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1110,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"178 O Yudhishthira! Brave ones, aryas and those who are learned must be treated well.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":25,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1320,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! The lord has honoured the devarshis, with Brihaspati at the forefront, and having satisfied them, has studied policy.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":38,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2373,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kumara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In ancient times, he studied the truth about transcendental paths from Kumara, the eldest son of the grandfather, who blazed in his energy.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":38,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2377,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bharadvaja","Brahma","Indra","Kavya","Manu","Prachetasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The large- eyed and illustrious Kavya, the great ascetic,547 the thousand-eyed and great Indra, Manu, the son of Prachetasa, the illustrious Bharadvaja and the sage Gourashira were devoted to Brahma and learned about the brahman.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":58,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3668,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among kings! O lord of the earth! That is the reason the learned pronounce that on earth, gods and human gods are similar.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":59,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3927,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In every way, shame on a state without a king! The learned texts say that Indra is crowned in the form of a king.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":67,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4346,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1402(74) \u2018Bhishma said, \u201cThe king must consider both dharma and artha and their differences, which are often unfathomable, and then appoint a priest who is extremely learned in the sacred texts.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":74,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4810,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["King"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"When King Muchukunda, the scorcher of enemies, saw that his own soldiers were being slaughtered, he censured his learned priest.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":75,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4897,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Narada","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cVasudeva said, \u2018O Narada! A person who is not a well-wisher should not get to know the supremely secret counsel, nor should a well-wisher who is not learned, or a learned person who is not in control of his soul.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":82,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5260,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"769 O Kounteya! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! For all tasks, choose as aides those who are extremely wealthy, extremely brave, extremely learned brahmanas, those who are extremely satisfied with you and capable of great enterprise.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":84,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5448,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Nahusha","Yayati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Yayati, the son of Nahusha, declared this teaching for kings.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":94,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6061,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Nabhaga"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"861 O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Nabhaga gave away the kingdoms and the kings as dakshina, with the exception of what belonged to learned brahmanas and ascetics.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":97,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6170,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1438(110) \u2018Yudhishthira asked, \u201cO descendant of the Bharata lineage! If a man wishes to base himself on dharma, how should he conduct himself? O learned one! O bull among the Bharata lineage! I wish to know.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":110,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6995,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1443(115) \u2018Yudhishthira asked, \u201cO descendant of the Bharata lineage! O scorcher of enemies! How should a learned and mild man behave, when he is abused in an assembly by someone who is stupid, voluble and harsh?\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cO protector of the earth! Listen to what has been sung about this objective.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":115,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7335,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cIf all the servants are learned about jnana and vijnana, if they seek welfare, if they are born in good lineages and if they are gentle, then that kingdom obtains the fruits.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":116,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7394,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among men! In this way, with brave, wise and extremely learned people, who are born in noble lineages, one is capable of conquering the entire earth.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":119,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7524,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brihaspati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018O king! You have studied all of Brihaspati\u2019s doctrines.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":122,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7750,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1462(134) \u2018Bhishma said, \u201cThose who are learned about the ancient accounts chant a verse that was sung by Brahma himself.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":134,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8495,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kounteya! Therefore, resort to the intelligence used by learned people in determining dharma and adharma.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":139,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9537,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cOne must always serve learned and aged brahmanas and ascetics and also those who are firm and pure in their learning, character and conduct.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":140,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9612,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Goutama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Goutama made supreme efforts to learn archery.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":162,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11202,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019\u201d \u2018Bhishma said, \u201cThe learned brahmana mentioned these and other reasons.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":168,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11591,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kashyapa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kashyapa! You are a human and a learned brahmana.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":173,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11972,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhrigu"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018\u201cBhrigu replied, \u2018Those who are engaged in following their own dharma are learned.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":184,"cited":true,"sentence_id":12555,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Arishtanemi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Some learned ones know him as Arishtanemi.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":201,"cited":true,"sentence_id":13822,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Duhsaha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"I am known as Duhsaha and the learned know me as Vidhitsa.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":218,"cited":true,"sentence_id":14957,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shuka","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Vyasa\u2019s son, Shuka, studied all the Vedas, Vedangas and Upanishads and having become accomplished about the knowledge of dharma, wished to find out about virtuous deeds.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":224,"cited":true,"sentence_id":15669,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shuka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cShuka asked, \u2018There may be a learned brahmana who has had offspring.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":231,"cited":true,"sentence_id":16178,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Svaha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned say that if a person has sacrificed to the best of his capacity and has uttered the words \u201cOm\u201d, the womb of the brahman, \u201cNamah\u201d, \u201cSvaha\u201d, \u201cSvadha\u201d and \u201cVashat\u201d, he has nothing to fear in the three worlds and in the world hereafter.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":260,"cited":true,"sentence_id":18015,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Vritra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"When he spoke in this way, the illustrious Ushanas replied, \u2018O son!624 Why are you speaking these terrible, wicked and insane words?\u2019 \u2018\u201cVritra said, \u2018You and the other learned ones have directly seen the great austerities I tormented myself with in earlier times and the sacrifices that I performed out of greed.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":270,"cited":true,"sentence_id":18705,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cThe worship of seniors, serving the aged and listening to the learned and the superior\u2014these are said to be the best.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":276,"cited":true,"sentence_id":19237,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Prajapati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Those who are learned about dharma know that when Prajapati created the worlds, some were created from his mouth, some from his arms, some from his thighs and some from his feet.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":285,"cited":true,"sentence_id":19779,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Videha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O ruler of Videha! O great king! Learned ones say that shudras are like brahmanas.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":285,"cited":true,"sentence_id":19811,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Janaka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019\u201d \u2018Bhishma said, \u201cO king! The learned one thus spoke about the truth to Janaka.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":287,"cited":true,"sentence_id":20005,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cO lord! The learned have said that there are five faults in the body.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":290,"cited":true,"sentence_id":20292,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among men! Asked by you, I have now told you exactly what I learned.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":296,"cited":true,"sentence_id":20988,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Lomaharshana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"I then studied the Puranas from Lomaharshana.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":306,"cited":true,"sentence_id":21409,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The great rishis who dwell in Brahma\u2019s abode say that Aditya, the eternal lord of all those who give heat, taught you about this.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":306,"cited":true,"sentence_id":21478,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kapila","Shuka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Shuka, supreme among those who know about the brahman, accepted the instructions of his father and studied the sacred texts of yoga and everything propounded by Kapila.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":312,"cited":true,"sentence_id":22272,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Parashara","Vyasa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018\u201cOn the slopes of those mountains, Vyasa, Parashara\u2019s immensely ascetic son, taught the Vedas.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":314,"cited":true,"sentence_id":22508,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Agni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned have thus come to think of brahmanas as Agni.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":329,"cited":true,"sentence_id":24371,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma","Pushkara","Satya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"In Pushkara, in Brahma\u2019s abode, the learned rishis addressed me as Satya.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":330,"cited":true,"sentence_id":24605,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Panchala","Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Using fierce austerities, the rishi Panchala worshipped the god who assumed the form of Hayashira and learnt shiksha, following the path instructed by Rama.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":335,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25154,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Soma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"1320 Then, the grandfather obtained and learned this dharma from Soma.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25232,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Rudra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! In that ancient krita yuga, Rudra immersed himself in yoga and taught this dharma to all the Valakhilya rishis.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25234,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Manu","Svarochisha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"For the welfare of the worlds and for the sake of establishing this dharma, he then taught it to Svarochisha Manu.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25269,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shankhapada","Svarochisha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"1326 O king! In ancient times, Svarochisha, the lord and protector of all the worlds, himself carefully taught it to his son, Shankhapada.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25270,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shankhapada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Shankhapada taught it to his son Sudharma, the protector of the directions.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25271,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanatkumara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! The illustrious Sanatkumara studied it.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25275,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Prajapati","Sanatkumara"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O tiger among the Kuru lineage! From Sanatkumara, at the beginning of krita yuga, Prajapati Virana obtained this dharma and studied it.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":336,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25276,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Brahma! Create many kinds of subjects, those who are learned and those who are dumb.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":337,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25401,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among the serpents! I have learnt the truth about this through your instructions.","parva":"12_Shanti","chapter":347,"cited":true,"sentence_id":25819,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sudarshana"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Oghavat gave his daughter, Oghavati, who was as beautiful as a goddess, to the learned Sudarshana as a wife.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":2,"cited":true,"sentence_id":245,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Brahma and the other gods and learned maharshis praise, worship and honour you.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":17,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1942,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Yudhishthira asked, \u201cA person whom one has not met before, a learned person, a person who is related through marriage, an ascetic and a person who is devoted to sacrifices\u2014why are these regarded as worthy recipients of a gift?\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cNoble lineage, devotion to tasks, learning, non-violence, modesty, uprightness and truthfulness\u2014the foremost recipients possess at least three of these attributes.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":23,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2408,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Agni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018\u201cAgni said, \u2018There may be a person who studies and thinks himself to be learned.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":23,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2413,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Yudhishthira said, \u201cO grandfather! Learned ones have said that dharma has many end objectives and many doors.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":23,"cited":true,"sentence_id":2422,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bali","Namuchi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned say that Shambara\u2019s maya, Namuchi\u2019s maya and that of Bali and Kumbhinasa, all of that exists in a woman.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":39,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3451,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kushika"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 \u2018\u201cKushika said, \u2018O illustrious one! The learned ones have held that the act of dwelling together is a dharma that should be practised only when a daughter has been given away in marriage.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":52,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4365,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"I have learnt how Krishna became the cause of his liberation.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":71,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5823,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dasharatha","Indra","Rama"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Indra told Dasharatha and Rama learnt it from his father.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":73,"cited":true,"sentence_id":5942,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Agni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"That is the reason Agni is said to represent all the gods and the learned rishis, who possess insight about the proofs of the Vedas.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":85,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6890,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Jamadagni"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Jamadagni\u2019s son! O one who knows about proof! The learned texts and the Vedas are proof of this.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":85,"cited":true,"sentence_id":6969,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d\u2019 Chapter 1769(88) udhishthira asked, \u201cO lord! Which is the object that, if donated to ancestors, becomes inexhaustible? What oblation lasts for many nights? Indeed, what is thought to last for an eternity?\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cO Yudhishthira! Those who are learned about funeral ceremonies have thought of oblations for funeral ceremonies.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":88,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7098,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Nachiketa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Know that they are the sanctifiers of the line\u2014one who knows about the three Nachiketa fires;182 one who knows about the five sacrificial fires; one who knows the three Suparnas;183 one who knows the six Vedangas; one who is the descendant of ancestors who knew about the brahman; one who knows about metres; one who knows about Jyeshtha Sama;184 one who is obedient to his mother and his father; one whose ancestors have been learned for ten generations; one who always has intercourse with his lawful wife when she is in season; one who is learned in the Vedas; and one who has bathed himself in vows.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":90,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7180,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Yudhishthira! The learned know that brahmanas are those who always follow the injunctions laid down by the rishis.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":90,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7216,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Agastya","Ambarisha","Angiras","Ashtaka","Bharadvaja","Bhrigu","Dilipa","Galava","Goutama","Jamadagni","Kashyapa","King","Nahusha","Narada","Parvata","Puru","Shibi","Shukra","Vasishtha","Vishvamitra","Yayati"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O king! There were Shukra, Angiras, the learned Kavi, Agastya, Narada, Parvata, Bhrigu, Vasishtha, Kashyapa, Goutama, Vishvamitra, Jamadagni, the rishi Galava, Ashtaka, Bharadvaja, Arundhati, the Valakhilyas, Shibi, Dilipa, Nahusha, Ambarisha, King Yayati, Dhundhumara and Puru.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":96,"cited":true,"sentence_id":7676,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Indra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Indra among kings! The learned say that in the world of the gods and in the world of men, a householder who practises good conduct obtains prosperity.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":103,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8113,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O \u2018Y Yudhishthira! Anything that remains, which I have refrained from stating, must be learnt from aged ones.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":107,"cited":true,"sentence_id":8854,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Bhishma replied, \u201cThe learned say that all the tirthas indeed possess qualities.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":111,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9228,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Krishna Dvaipayana, foremost among brahmanas and learned about dharma and artha, saw his extensive austerities and arrived there.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":120,"cited":true,"sentence_id":9870,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Some learned people say that Brahma was born from an egg.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":138,"cited":true,"sentence_id":11538,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned say that Brahma\u2019s first son was Dharma.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":148,"cited":true,"sentence_id":12303,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Vasudeva"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Having spoken these words to the learned Dhritarashtra, the mighty-armed Kourava addressed Vasudeva.","parva":"13_Anushasana","chapter":153,"cited":true,"sentence_id":12523,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Angiras"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned lord Angiras himself was the officiating priest at these sacrifices.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":4,"cited":true,"sentence_id":174,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bala","Indra","Vritra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O learned one! O slayer of Bala and Vritra! O Indra! Through your presence here, this sacrifice has become more resplendent.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":10,"cited":true,"sentence_id":541,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"83 O Partha! It is my view that a man who is not accomplished in consciousness, is not learned and has not cleansed his soul, will be confused about this and will find it extremely difficult to grasp it.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":19,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1156,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Brahma","Partha"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Partha! If they resort to this dharma, those with inferior births, women, vaishyas and shudras, also go to the supreme destination, not to speak of extremely learned brahmanas and kshatriyas, who are always devoted to their own dharma and to the object of obtaining Brahma\u2019s world.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":19,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1166,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Utanka"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d \u2018Utanka said, \u201cThose who are learned and accomplished in their insight about the dharma to be followed vis-\u00e0-vis friends say that one who behaves unfairly towards friends is like a thief.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":57,"cited":true,"sentence_id":3439,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Ulupi"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u201d Thus asked, the lord of Manipura bowed his head down and said, \u201cO learned one! Let Ulupi be asked.","parva":"14_Ashvamedhika","chapter":81,"cited":true,"sentence_id":4687,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Bhishma","Drona","Kripa","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2019 I was overcome by affection towards my son and did not heed the learned and beneficial words of Vidura, Bhishma, Drona and Kripa.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":114,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gandhari"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Though her sons have been slain, it is Gandhari who has taught me patience.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":5,"cited":true,"sentence_id":138,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Sanjaya","Vidura"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned Vidura and the suta, Sanjaya, followed him.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":302,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Gandhari","Kunti"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Gandhari, knowledgable about dharma, and the learned Kunti were honoured by their daughters-in-law with various items and also ate.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":306,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Kounteya"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Kounteya! You are learned.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":313,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Yudhishthira! You must always respect those who are learned and aged.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":315,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Yudhishthira"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"O Yudhishthira! The women must be properly protected through aged guards and these must have good conduct, be born in noble lineages and learned.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":334,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Shatayupa"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"So did Dvaipayana and his disciples, other learned siddhas and the aged rajarshi, Shatayupa, supremely devoted to dharma.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":26,"cited":true,"sentence_id":960,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Narada"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"They praised Narada\u2019s learned words.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":26,"cited":true,"sentence_id":993,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Those learned brahmanas conversed in this way with Dhritarashtra and then went away as they desired, along paths meant for those who are successful.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":27,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1028,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dharmaraja"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"The learned Dharmaraja wished to perform the rites and perform the acts of cremation there.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":33,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1254,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra","Gandhari","King"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"\u2018He went and met the learned King Dhritarashtra, who had performed his ablutions and was seated at ease, together with Gandhari.","parva":"15_Ashramavasika","chapter":34,"cited":true,"sentence_id":1294,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Krishna"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"Krishna is capable of countering everything in the three worlds, mobile and immobile, not to speak of a curse imposed by learned ones.","parva":"16_Mausala","chapter":9,"cited":true,"sentence_id":487,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null},{"names":["Dhritarashtra"],"teacher":null,"student":null,"text":"He was the learned Dhritarashtra.","parva":"18_Svargarohana","chapter":4,"cited":true,"sentence_id":273,"status":"source match","in_training_graph":null}];
